    "title"             "Knox Relay"
    "description"       "Server-side bridge mod for remote server management. Exports game state, inventory snapshots, player positions, progression and live character vitals, and processes item delivery and money deposit queues via file-based JSON communication. Provides /account register for linking a character to a website account."
    "changenote"        "[h1]1.11 — /account register actually reaches the mod[/h1]\n[b]Fixed[/b]\n[list]\n[*]/account register returned \"Unknown Command\". The command was being read off the chat box by replacing ISChat.onCommandEntered, but the game copies that function onto the text entry when the chat window is built — so the replacement changed a name nothing looks at again, and the command went to the server as an unrecognised one. The hook now goes on the text entry itself, which is what the game actually calls.\n[*]The chat box is re-hooked if the interface is rebuilt during a session, so the command does not quietly stop working after a respawn.\n[/list]\n[b]Notes[/b]\n1.10 shipped the whole feature with no way to trigger it, which from a player's side was indistinguishable from the mod not being installed. There is now a test that builds a chat box the same way the game does and fails if the hook lands anywhere the game will not call."
}
